From 1c3084f6df2b81caeb69420921ad9ea134543313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:39:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gridforge): screen crashed on the blank intake; add
 end-to-end smoke tests and CI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The suite passed 62 tests while `gridforge screen` crashed on the intake that
`gridforge init` had just produced. That is a test-design failure, not a bad
patch: every test exercised library functions, none ran the product.

FIXES

- reporting/screen.py: the data-gap table renders prose about an assumption, not
  report figures. A fallback like "100" tripped the bare-number guard that exists
  to stop an unprovenanced figure reaching a customer. Gap cells are now Lit, which
  is the explicit "this needs no provenance" marker. Same fix in the portfolio
  recommendation column.
- intake/loader.py: an empty project.client no longer renders as "Envelope Study — :".
  Blank client and reference fall back to "Unnamed client" and "—".
- cli.py: a missing file, a directory, malformed JSON or an unmatched shell glob now
  exit 2 with one line that says what to do. `portfolio halls/*.json` - which was in
  the README and does not exist - printed a FileNotFoundError traceback at the user.
- README and runbook: the portfolio example now points at examples/intake/*.json,
  the path that actually ships.

TESTS THAT WOULD HAVE CAUGHT IT (tests/test_cli_smoke.py, 22 new)

Every command in the README and the runbook, run through the real entry point, on
the real files, asserting no traceback:

- init -> gaps -> screen -> study on a BLANK intake, the worst input a client can
  hand back;
- screen and study for every shipped example, parametrised;
- all three ranking objectives;
- portfolio across every example, one model pack per hall;
- unmatched glob, missing file, directory-instead-of-file and malformed JSON each
  exit 2 with an explanation;
- the Makefile still carries the targets the runbook tells a founder to type.

Verified by reverting the screen fix: the smoke test fails, the other 62 still pass.
That is the point of it.

CI (.github/workflows/gridforge.yml)

Runs the suite on 3.11 and 3.13, then produces a screen and a study from the blank
intake, a screen and a study for every example, a portfolio across all of them, and
the reference project - and uploads the deliverables as build artefacts. A green
build means the commands in the runbook work.

84 tests pass, up from 62.

